Write a starter treerig.toml at the root of the Git repository you run it in,
naming the Compose file found there (compose.yaml if none), with a commented-out
service and hooks to fill in. It refuses to replace an existing treerig.toml. Run
`treerig config validate` afterwards. It reads no treerig.toml, so --config is
refused.

Usage:
  treerig init [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for init

Global Flags:
      --config string   path to treerig.toml (default: nearest above cwd)
  -V, --version         output the version number
